# Negative-control mutant — the contracts picker's typed text lands on the
# picker's OWN `query` leaf, not a `filters.name.like` branch its internal
# lookup query no longer declares (G1)
#
# Scenario it must flip: typing into the `schemas.contractPicker` Lookup
#   control's search box narrows the options `lookups.contract()` returns —
#   the term must reach the internal lookup's `useContractLookupQuerySchema()`
#   model at a leaf that schema actually declares.
# Mutation: `useContractPickerUischema`'s `searchScope` reverts to
#   `"filters.name.like"`. `useContractLookupQuerySchema()` declares only
#   `query` and `pagination` (no `filters` branch), so a typed term is
#   stripped by the schema's `additionalProperties: false` and the search
#   does nothing — the same dead control G1 found, on the internal lookup
#   this time rather than the list's own FilterBar.
#
# Apply with:  git apply <this file>   (run from repo root)
# Revert with: git apply -R <this file>
diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/contract.schemas.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/contract.schemas.ts
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/contract.schemas.ts
+++ b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/contract.schemas.ts
@@ -206,7 +206,7 @@
         options: {
           lookup: {
             service: lookups.contract,
-            searchScope: "query"
+            searchScope: "filters.name.like"
           },
           optionalText: ""
         }
